From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:41:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: Add SM8650 MDSS compatible

Add the SM8650 MDSS compatible to the clients list, so it also gets an
identity domain at boot, as SM8550 does since the previous patch.

When the bootloader chainloads another EFI application it leaves its
continuous splash scanning out at kernel entry. Without an identity
domain the MDSS stream is attached to an empty translating domain as
soon as the device is added, so the splash fetches fault until the DPU
driver stops the timing engine and attaches its own domain.

Signed-off-by: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 483e9e4..bd8ea02 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -427,6 +427,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8250-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8450-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-mdss" },
 	{ }
 };
